      "body": "\n# 2026-08-03\n\nBack from a week off, so the morning went to triage rather than anything clever. The repo behind [[Atlas Overview]] had drifted — three open branches nobody could describe in one sentence — and I closed two of them before standup. The [[Atlas kickoff]] meeting in the afternoon was better than I expected: scope came out smaller, not bigger, which almost never happens on day one.\n\nAna walked us through the onboarding funnel numbers. The drop-off is not where we assumed; people don't leave at the account step, they leave at the first empty screen. That reframes the whole epic.\n\n- [ ] Write the one-paragraph Atlas scope statement @project(Atlas) @due(2026-08-05) @status(todo)\n- [ ] Delete the two stale branches and note why in the changelog @due(2026-08-06) @status(review) @project(Atlas)\n- [ ] Read back through [[Offline-First UX]] before Thursday @start(2026-08-05) @status(backlog) @project(Harbor)\n\n#daily\n",
